# NLP Project – Meta 2: Question Classification (HUM vs LLM)

Classify questions as written by a human (HUM) or generated by an LLM.

## Setup

Requires Python 3.10+.

```powershell
# 1. Create the virtual environment
python -m venv .venv

# 2. Activate it (Windows PowerShell)
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

On Linux/macOS, activate with `source .venv/bin/activate` instead.

If PowerShell blocks the activation script, run this once:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned
```

## Check that it works

Run from the project root:

```powershell
python src\check_data.py
```

The first run can take a while (importing scikit-learn is slow on a fresh environment). Wait for it to finish.

## Structure

```
data/      TSV files provided by the teachers
src/       shared code (data.py loads the data and creates the CV folds)
results/   results of each model (CSV)
notebooks/ exploration
```

Always load data through `src/data.py` so both of us use the same labels and the same folds.